% nodes_at — the nodes of a mesh that lie on a coordinate plane (x, y or z = value)
%
% Usage:      nodes = nodes_at(m, axis, value)          axis 1 (x), 2 (y) or 3 (z)
%             nodes = nodes_at(m, axis, value, tol)     tol: distance accepted (default 1e-6 × the mesh size)
%             tip = nodes_at(v, 1, 100);                the x = 100 end of a voxel cantilever
% Computes:   the 1-based numbers of the nodes used by at least one element whose coordinate along `axis` is
%             within tol of `value`, as a column. Voxel meshes number every grid node (as PartCraft's voxel.js
%             does); nodes no element uses are left out, so the list can be held or loaded directly.
% Method:     meshNodes, meshElems, a mask. Pure script.
% Units:      the mesh's length unit.
% Limits:     planes only; for curved faces of tet meshes use face_nodes.
% References: none needed (a selection helper); node numbering as cs-lib-mesh.js / voxel.js.
% Check:      used by every static, modal and thermal check (bin/test-craftscript.mjs --lib): the voxel box
%             100 × 10 × 10 at h = 2.5 has (4+1)·(4+1) = 25 nodes on x = 0.
function nodes = nodes_at(m, axis, value, tol)
X = meshNodes(m);
if nargin < 4
  tol = 1e-6 * max(max(X) - min(X));
end
used = false(size(X, 1), 1);
E = meshElems(m);
used(E(:)) = true;
nodes = find(used & abs(X(:, axis) - value) <= tol);
end
